==Reactions==
Several analysts have raised concerns that Pinto da Costa's victory may trigger a return to the authoritarian rule seen during his previous period in power.<ref>{{Cite news|author=Felix, Bate|author2=Neto, Ricardo |title=Sao Tome's Pinto da Costa wins presidential runoff|url=https://af.reuters.com/article/energyOilNews/idAFL6E7J818Q20110808|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120926020916/http://af.reuters.com/article/energyOilNews/idAFL6E7J818Q20110808|url-status=dead|archive-date=26 September 2012|date=8 August 2011|access-date=8 August 2011|agency=Reuters}}</ref>

